# Martin's Web: design system rules

This site is built from the design system in `design-system/`. It is the source of truth for how anything looks, reads and behaves. Do not invent styles.

## Before touching any UI

1. Read `design-system/README.md` (the brand book: voice, colour, type, spacing, layout, page patterns). Read it again whenever you build a new page or pattern.
2. For a component, read `design-system/components/<Name>/README.md`, its props in `design-system/components/index.d.ts`, and its usage in `design-system/components/<Name>/example.html`.
3. For a page, open its approved design in `design-system/pages/` (see `design-system/pages/README.md`).
4. `design-system/reference/bundle.js` and `bundle.css` are the working React implementation of every component. Port their markup, class names and states into the site's own components. Do not import or ship the bundle.

If the README and a page design in `design-system/pages/` disagree, the page design wins (it is the final canvas, Nov 2026); the designer's notes are in `design-system/pages/NOTES.md`. If something is not covered, ask instead of guessing.

## Tokens

- Import `design-system/tokens.css` once, globally. It defines every token as a CSS custom property, plus `.type-*` classes for the type scale.
- Colours, spacing, radii, shadows and layout widths always come from `var(--token)`. Never hard-code a hex, rgb or px value that a token covers.
- Paint with semantic tokens (`surfaces-*`, `text-*`, `button-*`, `accent`, `highlight-rule`, `topic-*`). Never use the primitives (`teal-*`, `mint-500`, `neutral-*`) directly in components.
- Type: use the `.type-<name>` classes (`display`, `h1` to `h4`, `body`, `body-long`, `pull-quote`, `highlights`, `button`, `caption`, `caption-mono`). They switch to the mobile scale below 600px on their own.
- `tokens.css` is generated from `tokens.json`. Never edit it by hand.
- Fonts are self-hosted: `tokens.css` imports `design-system/fonts.css`, which loads the files in `design-system/fonts/`. Do not add Google Fonts links or other families.

## Theme

- Light is the default. Dark is opt-in only, through an explicit toggle that sets `data-theme="dark"` on `<html>` and remembers the reader's choice.
- Never switch theme from `prefers-color-scheme`.
- Components need no theme-specific code: the semantic tokens already change.

## Layout

- Breakpoints: 600 (`breakpoint-sm`, phone type and spacing), 768 (`breakpoint-md`, header nav collapses, hero stacks), 1024 (`breakpoint-lg`, desktop gutter).
- Content lives in a centred `container-max` (1440px) with `gutter-lg` / `gutter-md` / `gutter-sm` side padding.
- No text block wider than `measure-page` (800px). Article bodies use `measure-reading` (680px).
- One left edge per page. Indent only content hanging from a rail.

## Shape and depth

- `radius-s` (4px) for Buttons, Chips and Inputs; `radius-none` for structure (header, footer, Next-Read cards, forms); `radius-card` (8px) only for Cards. Avatars stay round. No pills.
- One shadow in use: `shadow-elevation`. No gradients.

## Icons and logo

- Only the eight glyphs in `design-system/assets/icons/` (share, quote, back, group, psychology, coach, external-link, menu). Inline them so they inherit `currentColor`. No icon libraries, no emoji.
- Logo: `design-system/assets/logo/martin-mato-logo.svg`. Inline it with the block M in `var(--text-primary)` and the script m in `var(--teal-500)` so it survives the dark theme. Always next to "Martín Mato" in Source Serif 4 Bold 30.

## Photos

- Use the photos in `design-system/assets/photos/` (described in `design-system/pages/README.md`). Never stock images or placeholders presented as real.
- Show Martín once per page. Heroes prefer a natural photo in context (the Kaizen booth); the post author block uses `portrait-headshot.jpg`.
- Every photo gets an explicit size with `object-fit: cover` and a real `alt`.

## Content rules

- Posts are written in English, first person, never prescriptive. Post titles in sentence case; page and section titles in title case.
- Topics are a closed list, in this order: Personal, Leading Teams, Mentoring, AI in Teams. One topic per post.
- Meta line is always: topic Chip, date, read time, joined by a middle dot "·" ("Sept 9, 2026 · 6 min read").
- No cover images on posts.
- A post page is exactly: Header, Article (author block, `body-long` paragraphs, at most one Highlight, ClosingPrompt), the dark newsletter band (`id="newsletter"`), Footer. Nothing else between them.
- Blog list: newest first, PostCards separated by `surfaces-divider` rules, "Older Entries" secondary Button for paging, never infinite scroll.

## Accessibility

- Real `<button>`, `<a href>`, `<input>` with `<label>`. Never click handlers on divs.
- Text 4.5:1 against its background (3:1 at 24px and up). The README lists the few pairs kept below that on purpose; do not add new ones.
- Focus rings: 1px `button-mid`, offset 2 to 3px. Touch targets at least 44px.
